# Scratch output in the REPO ROOT only — a chart saved while experimenting
# (event_study/plot.py hands back a figure; the caller saves it), a scratch
# note, an exported paper.
#
# These are deliberately root-anchored with a leading slash. They used to be
# repo-wide `*.png`, `*.txt`, `*.pdf`, which silently swallowed
# hedge_fund/features/snapshot_render_golden.txt: the golden-prompt test
# passed locally, because the file was on disk, and would have failed on a
# fresh clone. A blanket extension rule in a package that ships data files
# eats test fixtures, docs images, and requirements.txt without a word.
# Keep new ignores anchored to a directory.
/*.png
/*.pdf

# No `*.txt` rule, deliberately. The only .txt this project emits is
# ~/.hedge-fund/logs/candidates-<date>.txt, which is outside the repo, so a
# rule here guarded nothing — while quietly eating the golden-prompt fixture
# and standing ready to eat requirements.txt or a data file next.

# Outputs
outputs/
/scratchpad/

# Personal fund mandates and caches (live in ~/.hedge-fund/ now; stale
# sessions running pre-2.1 code may still write here)
/mandates/
.hedge_fund_cache/

# Local-only release tooling
scripts/release.sh
